<title>USA: N.H. education bonds repriced, yields lowered.</title>
<headline>N.H. education bonds repriced, yields lowered.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney Inc said Thursday it repriced New Hampshire Higher Educational and Health Facilities Authority's $24.6 million bond issue, lowering the 2012 and 2018 maturities to 5.88 percent and 5.98 percent, respectively.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>NEW HAMPSHIRE HIGHER EDUCATIONAL</p>
<p>AND HEALTH FACILITES AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $24,555,000*</p>
<p>REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>KENDAL AT HANOVER ISSUE SERIES 1997</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>THE ACCOUNT IS CLOSED.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: NR		  S&amp;P: A</p>
<p>				     LOC :BANK OF IRELAND, NY BRANCH</p>
<p>    DATED: 03/01/1997	  FIRST COUPON: 04/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 10/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
